  "worked_solution": "The coordinates of the point are $(2,6).$\n\n- The real part of this complex number is $x=2,$ and\n\n- the imaginary part is $y=6.$\n\nTherefore, the number depicted is $z=2+6i.$ Finally, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =2+6i \\\\  & =6\\,i+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
